WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:12.660
Something can't “be on fire”. Fire can
only be on things.

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:18.449
The US Patent Office insisted on proof that
the Ouija board worked before granting the

00:00:18.449 --> 00:00:23.609
patent in 1891.
In the Second World War, British troops were

00:00:23.609 --> 00:00:29.019
issued with three sheets of toilet paper a
day; American soldiers got 22.

00:00:29.019 --> 00:00:35.770
88% of women routinely wear shoes that are
too small for their feet.

00:00:35.770 --> 00:00:43.969
Seven US Presidents were born in log cabins.
A 1571 law stated that all Englishmen must

00:00:43.969 --> 00:00:49.739
wear knitted hats on Sundays.
There are more marijuana dispensaries in Denver,

00:00:49.739 --> 00:00:56.210
Colorado, than there are branches of Starbucks.
Before erasers were invented, breadcrumbs

00:00:56.210 --> 00:01:01.199
were used to rub out mistakes.
If you tickle a rat every day, it'll start

00:01:01.199 --> 00:01:07.060
laughing as soon as it sees you.
People with higher incomes generally prefer

00:01:07.060 --> 00:01:12.630
their loo paper to unravel over the roll,
while those with lower incomes prefer it to

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:17.159
go under.
The opening ceremony of the Beijing Olympics

00:01:17.159 --> 00:01:21.900
was the first time a billion people have watched
a sporting event.

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:27.860
Croquet was dropped as an Olympic sport after
1900 because only one spectator turned up

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:32.850
to watch.
It's impossible to set fire to a pool of petrol

00:01:32.850 --> 00:01:38.110
by throwing a lit cigarette into it. It's
also really, really unlikely that shooting

00:01:38.110 --> 00:01:42.780
the fuel tank of a vehicle will cause it to
explode. It's just not as easy as the movies

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:50.329
make it out to be.
In 2007 Scotland spent £125,000 to develop

00:01:50.329 --> 00:01:56.509
a new national slogan. The winning entry was
"Welcome to Scotland".

00:01:56.509 --> 00:02:01.079
The Milky Way gives birth to a new star every
50 days.

00:02:01.079 --> 00:02:08.989
Everyone has at least 50,000 thoughts a day
but 95% of them are the same as the day before.

